  "verses": {
    "verse": [
      [
        "When we walk with the Lord in the light of His Word,",
        "what a glory He sheds on our way!",
        "While we do His good will, He abides with us still,",
        "and with all who will trust and obey."
      ],
      [
        "Not a shadow can rise, not a cloud in the skies,",
        "but His smile quickly drives it away;",
        "not a doubt nor a fear, not a sigh nor a tear,",
        "can abide while we trust and obey."
      ],
      [
        "Not a burden we bear, not a sorrow we share,",
        "but our toil He doth richly repay;",
        "not a grief nor a loss, not a frown nor a cross,",
        "but is blest if we trust and obey."
      ],
      [
        "But we never can prove the delights of His love",
        "until all on the altar we lay;",
        "for the favor He shows, and the joy He bestows,",
        "are for them who will trust and obey."
      ],
      [
        "Then in fellowship sweet we will sit at His feet,",
        "or we'll walk by His side in the way;",
        "what He says we will do, where He sends we will go;",
        "never fear, only trust and obey."
      ]
    ]
  },
  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1 and refrain, soprano (melody) line, verified against the Mutopia LilyPond score (the score's repeated-phrase macro is written out). No simplification needed. Range 1 to 6. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–5: John H. Sammis (1887) as printed in The Army and Navy Hymnal (1920), from Wikisource (https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Army_and_Navy_Hymnal/Hymns/When_We_Walk_with_the_Lord); 'not a grief nor a loss' reads the transcription's 'Nor a grief not a loss' as the parallel 'not … nor' of the rest of the line. The refrain is sung after every verse.",
  "verified": true
}
